# main { try { mid(); } catch (A) } -> mid { try { skip(); } catch (B) + a cleanup }
# -> skip { a context, but call_site = -1 at the call } -> leaf { cleanup } -> throw A.
# Phase 1 passes leaf (cleanup only), skip (no call site) and mid (B does not match A)
# and finds main. Phase 2 runs leaf's cleanup, which resumes; skips skip; runs mid's
# cleanup (selector 0), which resumes; and installs main's handler (selector 1).
# main's LSDA uses the game's type encoding 0x9B (indirect | pcrel | sdata4), mid's the
# game's call-site header (encoding 3, a padded ULEB128 length).
title: nested contexts: cleanups, a non-matching handler and a skipped frame unwind to the outer handler
ref: GCC unwind-sjlj.c (phase 2 calls each personality with _UA_CLEANUP_PHASE, a context with call_site -1 has none); libsupc++ eh_personality.cc (a cleanup in the action chain); ADR 0020

[code]
